<title>DUBAI: VLCC World Champion berthed at Iraq's Mina al-Bakr.</title>
<headline>VLCC World Champion berthed at Iraq's Mina al-Bakr.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Liberian-flagged and Japanese-owned crude tanker World Champion has berthed at Iraq's Mina al-Bakr oil export terminal in the northern Gulf, Gulf shipping sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tanker is the third vessel to arrive at Mina al-Bakr under the United Nations &quot;oil-for-food&quot; deal with Baghdad.</p>
<p>Gulf shipping sources said the tanker would stay at Mina al-Bakr for at least three days to load its cargo of Iraqi Basrah Light crude.</p>
<p>The first two cargoes of Iraqi oil from Mina al-Bakr were exported by American firms Coastal Corp and Bayoil on December 17 and December 19.</p>
<p>World Champion's charterer was not immediately known.</p>
<p>-- Steven Swindells, Dubai Newsroom, +971 4 6071255.</p>
